Bugfix: Avoid repeated retries for truncated files with the rclone backend

When repairing a truncated pack, restic retried every inaccessible part several
times with the rclone backend. Restic now remembers a file's persistent failure
for one hour and avoids repeating those retries for later permanent errors.
Readable parts are still recovered, and temporary errors still retry normally.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/5530
